 The list of discovered PuppetDB targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.puppetdbSDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
 
+## scaleway_sd_configs
+
+Scaleway SD configuration discovers scrape targets from [Scaleway](https://www.scaleway.com/) Instances.
+
+Configuration example:
+
+```yaml
+scrape_configs:
+- job_name: scaleway
+  scaleway_sd_configs:
+
+    # secret_key is sent as the `X-Auth-Token` header value in every HTTP API request during service discovery (mandatory).
+    # See: https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/identity-and-access-management/iam/how-to/create-api-keys/
+  - secret_key: "..."
+
+    # zones is an optional list of Scaleway zones to query for instances.
+    # See: https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/#regions-and-zones
+    #
+    # zones: ["fr-par-1", "nl-ams-1"]
+    # By default, only the "fr-par-1" zone is queried.
+
+    # project_id is an optional filter for instances belonging to the given project.
+    #
+    # project_id: "..."
+
+    # organization_id is an optional filter for instances belonging to the given organization.
+    #
+    # organization_id: "..."
+
+    # port is an optional port to scrape metrics from.
+    # By default, port 80 is used.
+    #
+    # port: ...
+
+    # Additional HTTP API client options can be specified here.
+    # See https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#http-api-client-options
+```
+
+Each discovered target has an [`__address__`](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/#how-to-modify-scrape-urls-in-targets) label set
+to `<ip>:<port>`, where `<ip>` is the instance's public IP address (or its private IP address if it has no public IP) and `<port>`
+is the port from the `scaleway_sd_configs` (default port is `80`). Instances without any IP address are skipped.
+
+The following meta labels are available on discovered targets during [relabeling](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/):
+
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_id`: the unique ID of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_name`: the name of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_hostname`: the hostname of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_zone`: the [zone](https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/#regions-and-zones) in which the Instance is located.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_state`: the power state of the Instance, e.g. `running`, `stopped`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_commercial_type`: the commercial type (offer) of the Instance, e.g. `DEV1-S`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_project_id`: the ID of the project the Instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_organization_id`: the ID of the organization the Instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ip`: the public IPv4 address of the Instance, if any.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_private_ip`: the private IPv4 address of the Instance, if any.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_tags`: comma-separated list of tags applied to the Instance.
+
+Use relabeling if only `running` instances must be scraped, for example:
+
+```yaml
+relabel_configs:
+- source_labels: [__meta_scaleway_instance_state]
+  regex: running
+  action: keep
+```
+
+The list of discovered Scaleway targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.scalewaySDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
+
 ## static_configs
 
 A static config allows specifying a list of targets and a common label set for them.
